26, the house that published nineteen of the works recorded here, among them the songs Kaper wrote between 1929 and 1931 — the years of Robinson’s three texts for him. The group is the same circle photographed in Vienna for Die Bühne the same summer. The photograph itself is a coarse newspaper halftone in which no face can be told from another, so it does not settle which figure in the Vienna photograph is Robinson; the page is cited for its caption.","researchNoteType":"evidence_note","slug":"src0901-die-stunde-1926-whiteman-berlin-robinson","organizationIds":["ORG029","ORG064"],"personIds":["P083"],"primaryUrl":"https://anno.onb.ac.at/cgi-content/anno?aid=std&datum=19260701&seite=7"}],"media":[],"works":[],"films":[],"songs":[],"otherWorks":[],"titleVariants":[],"workRelations":[],"timelineEvents":[],"places":[],"contributions":[],"personNameVariants":[]}}
